      "heading": "What Is Gluco Shield Pro Diet Plan and How Does It Affect Blood Sugar?",
      "body": "<p>Gluco Shield Pro diet plan is a structured eating approach that prioritizes low‑glycemic index foods, high‑fiber vegetables, and moderate protein to stabilize blood sugar. It is not a medication; instead, it uses nutrition to influence the body’s insulin response and glucose production.</p>\n<h3>Mechanism</h3>\n<p>The plan reduces rapid glucose absorption by limiting refined carbohydrates and sugary foods. Fiber slows gastric emptying, which helps maintain steady blood glucose levels. Adequate protein supports muscle maintenance and improves insulin sensitivity, while healthy fats contribute to satiety and help blunt post‑meal spikes.</p>\n<h3>Secondary Effects</h3>\n<p>Beyond blood sugar control, the diet promotes weight management, lowers LDL cholesterol, and may reduce inflammation. These benefits are consistent with findings from Mediterranean‑style diets that emphasize plant‑based foods and healthy fats.</p>\n<h3>Research Note</h3>\n<p>A 2022 study of an Italian Ketogenic Mediterranean Diet in overweight and obese patients with prediabetes or type 2 diabetes found significant improvements in fasting glucose and glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c), supporting the effectiveness of low‑GI, high‑fiber approaches (Ivan et al., 2022).</p>\n",
